Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:56:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 147/174] fix: a CineCam Grade that cannot reach the picture
 now says why (S10 item 2b)

The report after 857f1e15 was "Slope 1.2 and Saturation 0.5 on the new
component do nothing at all". The editor log of that session says why, and it
is not the component binding: the camera was on the STOCK path.

Root cause of "no effect"
  The ASC CDL and the LMT are read by the tone map inside `if (bSceneReferred)`
  (ToneMapping.cpp, the camera grading block) - with Scene Referred off the
  renderer never looks at Global_User_Grade*, so a grade is inert by
  construction, exactly as it was before the component existed. The session's
  camera was created in that session with "Create Cinematic Camera", and
  SCineSceneReferredParams::bSceneReferred defaults to false. Evidence in
  editor.log (10 Sep 01:20-01:23): the "[CinematicCamera] WB ... gains ..."
  lines at 01:22:18-20 are only reachable AFTER ApplyWhiteBalance's
  `if (m_sceneReferred.bSceneReferred) return;`, "[SceneReferred] stock mid
  grey armed" is the stock-path arming, and none of the renderer's
  "request flipped -> " / "starts scene-referred" lines is in the file. The
  component lookup itself is proven good by the same log: the editor host's
  component audit lists CCineGradeComponent with classDesc GUID
  1e7c4a93-6b25-4d8f-9a03-52d7f1c86b40, which is what
  IEntity::GetComponent<T>() matches on.

  So the defect is not arithmetic, it is that the pothole became invisible.
  Before the move, Grade sat two groups under the Scene Referred switch on one
  inspector; now it is a separate component whose inspector shows no trace of
  the switch it depends on, and a value that cannot reach the picture said
  nothing at all.

What this adds
  - CCineGradeComponent::ReportStatus(): on its own PROPERTY_CHANGED it names,
    in ONE warning, every reason an edited value cannot be in the picture - no
    Cinematic Camera on the entity, the viewport not looking through it while
    editing (the S9 preview policy), the camera's Scene Referred switch off -
    and logs one line when the grade IS live. De-duplicated on the message, so
    dragging a slider says it once, and re-armed when the answer changes.
  - CCinematicCameraComponent::ApplyGrade() logs the CDL it publishes whenever
    the values change, edge-triggered exactly like the white balance line
    beside it. That splits "the value never left the component" from "the
    value is on the bus and the chain below is where to look" without a
    debugger.
  - CCinematicCameraComponent::IsSceneReferred(), a const accessor for the
    switch, which is what the grade component asks.
  - The component's editor description and README name the switch.

Also: the grade component no longer subscribes to ENTITY_EVENT_LEVEL_LOADED or
ENTITY_EVENT_START_GAME. They existed only to print the "no camera" warning at
load, which ReportStatus now covers where the user is looking, and a component
that holds state and answers questions has no business on the game-mode event
path. This is NOT a proven cause of the second report (the editor froze on
Ctrl+G): that session was the first game-mode entry into airfield in months and
the log stops immediately after CryAgentEditorHost auto-started four agentscript
behaviours, with nothing of this component's between. Narrowing the surface is
free; the freeze still needs an A/B and a hang dump.

Behaviour of the picture is unchanged: no bus write, no gate, no default moved.

